Panels of velvet. Dated late 16th–early 17th century. Cut and uncut voided silk velvet. a) L. 55 1/4 x W. 28 1/4 inches (140.3 x 71.8 cm);
b) L. 28 1/4 x W. 21 3/8 inches (71.8 x 54.3 cm);
c) L. 7 x W. 3 inches (17.8 x 7.6 cm);. Classified as Textiles-Velvets. Gift of Kate Read Blacque, in memory of her husband, Valentine Alexander Blacque, 1933.

Egyptomania candelabrum (one of a pair). Candelabrum and stand. Alexis Decaix. Dated ca. 1802–6. Gilded bronze. Overall (candelabrum (.1a–g), confirmed): 29 3/4 × 15 × 13 1/4 in., 42 lb. (75.6 × 38.1 × 33.7 cm, 19.1 kg);
Overall (stand (.2), confirmed): 3 1/2 × 14 5/8 × 14 5/8 in. (8.9 × 37.1 × 37.1 cm);
Length (longest branches): 8 1/2 in. (21.6 cm). Classified as Metalwork-Gilt Bronze. Purchase, Gift of Irwin Untermyer, by exchange, 2016.
